      "title": "Read me",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Why this graph looks like it does\n\nTwo things in the earlier version of these workflows could never have run, and\nboth were found by actually executing them:\n\n**1. The text encoder.** `ltx-2-3-22b-text_encoder.safetensors` is *not* a text\nencoder -- it holds four tensors, `text_embedding_projection.*`. LTX-2.3's text\nencoder is **Gemma-3-12B**, and the projection aggregates its 49 hidden states\n(49 x 3840 = 188160). `comfy/sd.py` only takes the LTX-2.3 Gemma branch\n(`ltxav_te` + `LTXAVGemmaTokenizer`, sd.py:1809) when handed **exactly two**\nstate dicts. A single-file `CLIPLoader(type=ltxv)` falls into the LTX-0.9 **T5**\nbranch instead and dies with `Cannot copy out of meta tensor`.\n\nSo: **`DualCLIPLoader`, type `ltxv`**, Gemma first (sd.py:1812 reads the\ntokenizer from `clip_data[0][\"spiece_model\"]`), projection second. Both live in\n`models/text_encoders`, so nothing is needed in `models/checkpoints`.\n\n**2. The audio branch is not optional.** `ltx-2.3-22b-dev` is an **AV** DiT.\n`av_model.py` builds audio RoPE unconditionally, so a video-only latent gives it\nzero audio tokens and it crashes in `freqs_cis_matrix`. Every upstream 2.3\nworkflow concatenates an audio latent for exactly this reason.\n`LTXVAudioVAELoader` lists from the (empty) `checkpoints` folder, but core\n`VAELoader` reads `models/vae` -- where `LTX23_audio_vae_bf16.safetensors` is.\nThe audio half is split back off and discarded here.\n\n## Measured on an RTX 3090 (Q4_0, 960x544x121, 20 steps, cfg 3.0)\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| wall clock | 230.8 s (11.04 s/step) |\n| peak VRAM | 20.9 GB of 24 GB |\n\nThat is tight. If it will not fit, see the tuning list in the folder README.\n\n## Want it 2.45x faster, and better looking?\n\nUse **`LTX-2.3_GGUF_T2V_Distilled_3090.json`** instead: a distilled LoRA at\n8 steps and cfg 1.0 renders this same clip in **94.3 s**, sharper than this\ngraph does in 230.8 s.\n\nAdding **LTXV Attention Backend** -> `sage` to *this* graph is worth only ~5%\n(230.8 -> 218.9 s). The step count is what matters, not the kernel.\n"
      ],
